        "file": "block/vmdk.c",
        "start_line": 876,
        "end_line": 877,
        "side": "new",
        "severity": "medium",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "Grain marker written without little-endian conversion",
        "explanation": "The reader uses le32_to_cpu(marker->size), but the writer stores lba and size in host byte order. On big-endian hosts the written compressed grains cannot be read back, and the image is corrupt for other tools. The lba field is also 64-bit, so it needs cpu_to_le64.",
        "suggestion": "Use data->lba = cpu_to_le64(sector_num); data->size = cpu_to_le32(buf_len);",
        "evidence": "data->size = buf_len;",
        "confidence": 0.6,
        "id": "69fd575dffa8",
        "hunk_id": "block/vmdk.c#2",
        "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
        "tier": 3,
        "escalated_from": [],
        "also_reported_by": []
      },
      {
        "file": "block/vmdk.c",
        "start_line": 937,
        "end_line": 937,
        "side": "new",
        "severity": "medium",
        "category": "security",
        "title": "Marker size bound ignores header; heap over-read",
        "explanation": "With has_marker set, the compressed data starts sizeof(VmdkGrainMarker) bytes into cluster_buf, which holds buf_bytes bytes. The check allows data_len up to buf_bytes, so a crafted image can make uncompress() read past the end of the heap buffer.",
        "suggestion": "Reject the size when data_len > buf_bytes - sizeof(VmdkGrainMarker) for marker extents.",
        "evidence": "if (!data_len || data_len > buf_bytes) {",
        "confidence": 0.6,
        "id": "b9b80496111a",
